---
/**
 * K Culture Wire — **어느 «언어판»에서 읽히나.** (`/read-in`)
 *
 * ── ⛔ 이 지면이 지키는 것 — 지우지 않는다 ──────────────────────────────────
 * ⛔ 「중국이 본다」로 쓰지 않는다 — zh.wikipedia 는 중국 본토에서 막혀 있다.
 *    이 한 줄을 빼면 지면이 거짓이 된다. 첫 화면 경고에 넣는다
 * ⛔ 「언어판 = 나라」가 아니다 — es 는 스페인과 중남미가 함께 읽는다
 * ⛔ 「인기」라 쓰지 않는다. 열람은 좋은 일로도 나쁜 일로도 는다
 * ⛔ en 을 1위 다툼에서 뺀 것을 «지면에 적는다». 숨기고 빼면 속임이다
 * ⛔ 「왜 그런가」를 말하지 않는다 — 화교 인구인지 편집 습관인지 우리 자료로 못 가른다
 * ⛔ 전수가 아니다 — 문턱(sitelinks 20)을 지면에 적는다
 * ⛔ 수를 손으로 적지 않는다. 전부 `kcw-language-reads.json` 에서 읽는다
 */
import WikiTip from '../../layouts/WikiTip.astro';
import KcwRelatedArticles from '../../components/KcwRelatedArticles.astro';
import data from '../../data/kcw-language-reads.json';

const 수 = (v) => (v == null ? '—' : Number(v).toLocaleString('en-US'));
const 표 = data.leadTable;
const 으뜸 = 표[0];
const 둘째 = 표[1];
const zh = data.zhOverJa;

const TITLE = `${으뜸.name}, not ${둘째.name}, leads for ${으뜸.leads} of ${data.people} Korean stars`;
const DESC =
  `Reads of ${data.people} Korean entertainers' Wikipedia articles across ${data.editions} language `
  + `editions, ${data.window}. Setting English aside, ${으뜸.name} is the most-read edition for `
  + `${으뜸.leads} of them and ${둘째.name} for ${둘째.leads}. Chinese Wikipedia is blocked in mainland China, `
  + `so these are language editions, not countries.`;

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Dataset',
  name: TITLE,
  description: DESC,
  temporalCoverage: String(data.window),
  creator: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'K Culture Wire' },
  isBasedOn: ['https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/', 'https://www.wikidata.org'],
  variableMeasured: ['Wikipedia page views by language edition'],
};

/* 이야기가 있는 판만 골라 낸다 — 1위가 열 명 미만인 판 */
const 좁은판 = 표.filter((x) => x.leads > 0 && x.leads < 20 && x.code !== 'en');
---

<WikiTip title={TITLE} description={DESC} jsonLd={jsonLd}
  canonical="https://www.kculturewire.com/read-in">
  <h1>{TITLE}</h1>

  <p class="lead">
    We asked Wikimedia how many people opened each of {수(data.people)} Korean entertainers'
    articles in each of {data.editions} language editions, over {data.window}. Every request came
    back — {data.blockedResponses} were blocked. English is set aside below, because our own site is
    in English and it would win every row.
  </p>

  <p class="warn">
    <b>These are language editions, not countries.</b> Chinese Wikipedia is blocked in mainland
    China, so its readers are in Taiwan, Hong Kong, Singapore, Malaysia and the wider diaspora.
    Spanish is read across Spain and Latin America. Read a row as “this language,” never as
    “this nation.”
  </p>

  {/* ⭐ [2026-09-09] 명부 요약을 «표»로 낸다. 앞서는 이 수들이 글 안에만 있어서
      표 약속 검사가 「478 이 표에 없다」고 세웠고, 그 말이 맞았다 —
      손님도 「이 표가 무엇을 담나」를 표로 보는 편이 낫다. */}
  <section>
    <h2>What this panel is</h2>
    <div class="scroll-x">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>What we counted</th><th>Number</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row">People measured</th><td class="tot">{수(data.people)}</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Language editions asked</th><td class="tot">{수(data.editions)}</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Person-edition cells</th><td class="tot">{수(data.people * data.editions)}</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Cells with no article at all</th><td class="tot">{수(data.cellsWithNoArticle)}</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Requests that came back blocked</th><td class="tot">{수(data.blockedResponses)}</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Wikipedia editions a person must have, to be here</th><td class="tot">{수(data.threshold)}</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="note">
      <b>Blocked requests are printed even though the answer is zero.</b> A count of zero
      blocked responses is what makes the empty cells meaningful: they are editions with no
      article, not requests that failed.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Which edition reads them most, with English set aside</h2>
    <div class="scroll-x">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Edition</th><th>People it leads for</th><th>Share</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {표.map((r) => (
            <tr class={r.code === 으뜸.code ? 'edge' : ''}>
              <td class="nm">{r.name}</td>
              <td class="tot">{수(r.leads)}</td>
              <td>{r.share}%</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="note">
      <b>Why English is set aside.</b> Every person here is read most in English, so leaving it in
      would produce one row and no information. We say so rather than quietly dropping it — the
      English count for each person is in the tables below.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>{zh.count} of them are read at least three times more in Chinese than in Japanese</h2>
    <div class="scroll-x">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Person</th><th>Chinese</th><th>Japanese</th><th>Times</th><th>English</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {zh.top.map((p) => (
            <tr>
              <td class="nm">{p.name}</td>
              <td class="tot">{수(p.zh)}</td>
              <td>{수(p.ja)}</td>
              <td class="tot">{p.times}×</td>
              <td class="fine">{수(p.english)}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="note">
      The rule is printed rather than tuned: {zh.rule}. {zh.count} people meet it. We do not say why —
      whether that reflects diaspora size, which stars are promoted where, or how each Wikipedia
      is written, nothing in this data separates those.
    </p>
  </section>

  {좁은판.map((판) => (
    <section>
      <h2>The {판.leads} read most in {판.name}</h2>
      <div class="scroll-x">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Person</th><th>{판.name}</th><th>Next edition</th><th>English</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            {data.leadersByEdition[판.code].map((p) => (
              <tr>
                <td class="nm">{p.name}</td>
                <td class="tot">{수(p.top)}</td>
                <td>{p.second ?? '—'}{p.secondReads == null ? '' : ` · ${수(p.secondReads)}`}</td>
                <td class="fine">{수(p.english)}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>
  ))}

  <section>
    <h2>Where we refuse to give a number</h2>
    <p class="note">
      <b>{수(data.cellsWithNoArticle)} person-edition cells have no article at all</b>, out of
      {' '}{수(data.people * data.editions)}. Those are left empty, not zero: an edition with no
      article is a different fact from an article nobody opened, and folding them together would
      make small editions look busier than they are.
    </p>
    <p class="note">
      <b>This is not the whole roster.</b> Only people whose Wikidata entry links to at least
      {' '}{data.threshold} Wikipedia editions are measured — {수(data.people)} of them. Someone with
      an article in two editions is absent here, which means this page describes widely
      documented people and not Korean entertainers in general.
    </p>
  </section>

  <KcwRelatedArticles page="/read-in" />

  <section class="src">
    <h2>Where these numbers come from, and what they cannot answer</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Wikimedia and Wikidata</b> — {data.source}</li>
      <li>
        <b>Views are attention, not liking.</b> A page climbs for good news and bad. We report the
        count and never the reason.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>Titles are resolved, never guessed.</b> Each edition's article title comes from Wikidata's
        sitelinks, so a Japanese title is the one Japanese Wikipedia actually uses.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>Bots are excluded</b> — the user-only series is used throughout.
      </li>
      <li><b>Window {data.window}. Built {data.builtOn}.</b> Whole months only; the current month is left out.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="note">
      <a href="/actors">The most looked-up Korean actors</a> ·{' '}
      <a href="/group-mix">Groups by who is in them</a> ·{' '}
      <a href="/about">How we count</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</WikiTip>
